## Drafted understanding (from the seed, before the reread)
The seed says a Builder can start when a batch is released, and that the work
book is the place for that job. Old packs and returns stay. Git had stored
different bytes from the installed files; Pack A caught it and Pack B tracked
the custody rule. `00.live` can be rebuilt and does not check that its names
resolve. Routine choices stay with Prime and Builder; an expected test refusal
is not a failure. The same page number in another book is not a collision.
The next runtime slice needs real code authority and new candidate versions.
Development batches stay distinct from a final reproducible `05`. The Workshop
paper is research, and no why book is allocated.

## Full reread
R01. `source-manifest.tsv` matched 13 of 13 before any edit, including the paper,
both returns, both Prime reports, the notes and the handoff report.
R02. Pack A return `#04`: the working copies were exact and the first remote
verification failed. 29 stored files differed. Cause recorded there: `* text=auto eol=lf`
with `core.autocrlf=true`. The failed log remains
`labs/bootstrap-preservation-pass01/evidence/verify-remote-first-FAIL.txt`.
The archived helper does not contain the later stored-blob check. Prime's Pack A
report accepts the preservation result and says the same.
R03. Pack B addendum `#B-A02` ran 6 of 6 gate tests. Refusals of CRLF-at-index,
a wrong staged blob, a mismatching commit and a local attributes override are
passes. `#B-A03` checked worktree, index, commit and fresh clones. The policy
in `.gitattributes` is the one the addendum names.
R04. Pack B `#02` kept its stops in `labs/bootstrap-establish-pass01/evidence/step02/attempts/`.
The handoff report kept `runs/initial-failure`. Prime's Pack B report kept the
first sandbox denial and says it is not a product regression. Those logs are the
untracked evidence folder staged unchanged.
R05. `render_live.py` accepts only the version-1 keys and the state words
`waiting`, `released`, `running`, `returned`, `accepted`, `stopped`. It refuses
